::CW_U02_L04_GP_Q01::Passage: "I set the cracked mug beside the new one and reached for the cracked one again." What is the literal meaning?{
~A. The narrator moves to a new city.#Incorrect. The passage does not mention moving.
~B. The narrator dislikes all mugs.#Incorrect. The narrator chooses a mug, so this is not supported.
=C. The narrator chooses an old cracked mug instead of a new mug.#Correct. Literal meaning states what directly happens on the surface.
~D. The narrator is definitely angry.#Incorrect. That is an unsupported inference.
}
::CW_U02_L04_GP_Q02::Passage: "The graduation banner stretched across the living room, but the suitcase by the stairs was already packed." Which evidence creates contrast?{
=A. The banner suggests celebration, while the packed suitcase suggests leaving.#Correct. The two details carry different emotional meanings, creating contrast.
~B. Both details show the same exact mood.#Incorrect. The point is that the details pull in different directions.
~C. The suitcase proves no one graduated.#Incorrect. The passage does not support that.
~D. The banner is not a detail.#Incorrect. The banner is an important detail.
}
::CW_U02_L04_GP_Q03::Passage: "Each morning, Mateo erased the calendar square before breakfast. On the last day, he left the marker uncapped beside the blank page." Which craft strategy is strongest?{
~A. Random decoration#Incorrect. The repeated erasing and changed ending are purposeful.
~B. Dialogue#Incorrect. No one speaks in the passage.
~C. Point of view shift#Incorrect. The passage does not shift perspective.
=D. Pattern#Correct. The repeated calendar action creates a pattern, and the final change adds meaning.
}
::CW_U02_L04_GP_Q04::Which explanation best supports an inference with evidence?{
~A. The detail means sadness because I say so.#Incorrect. This gives no evidence.
=B. The faded name suggests Leo's connection to the place is weakening because his name is disappearing but he still touches it.#Correct. This connects inference to specific evidence.
~C. The detail is deep.#Incorrect. This is too vague.
~D. The story has words.#Incorrect. This does not explain craft evidence.
}
::CW_U02_L04_GP_Q05::What is the best revision goal for adding layered meaning?{
~A. Make every detail mysterious even if the scene stops making sense.#Incorrect. The literal scene must stay clear.
~B. Remove all literal meaning.#Incorrect. Readers need a clear surface scene.
=C. Add one detail that has a clear surface role and a deeper implied role.#Correct. Layered details work on more than one level.
~D. Use only abstract words like sadness and change.#Incorrect. Concrete evidence makes inference possible.
}
